## The contract

**Use a token, never a raw colour in a component.** A colour that appears once
as `#dc2626` in one file is the colour nobody can change later.

{% if is_web %}
`static/app.css` holds the tokens, as CSS custom properties on `:root`. Add one
there before using it. Every token is defined on bare `:root` and only
*redefined* in the dark block, so no colour has its single definition inside a
media query.
{% else %}
`src/style.css` holds the tokens, in Tailwind v4's `@theme`. Add one there
before using it, and use the utility Tailwind generates from it — `bg-surface`,
`text-ink`, `border-line` — rather than a literal value.

The surface tokens are declared in `@theme inline`, which is the mechanism
rather than a detail: the generated utilities emit `var(--ui-surface)` instead
of resolving at build time, so swapping the variable flips the whole interface.
That is why not one generated component carries a `dark:` class, and adding one
is how the two themes start drifting apart.
{% endif %}

## Colour

{% if is_web %}
| Token | Use it for |
| --- | --- |
| `--accent` / `--accent-text` | The one action on the screen. `.btn-primary` is this pair |
| `--bg` | Page background |
| `--surface` | Cards, inputs, secondary buttons |
| `--border` | Dividers and outlines |
| `--text` | Body copy |
| `--muted` | Labels, hints, timestamps, empty-state copy |
| `--danger` | Destructive actions and error text |
| `--ok-bg` / `--ok-text`, `--off-bg` / `--off-text` | The two badge states |
{% else %}
| Token | Use it for |
| --- | --- |
| `brand-600` / `brand-500` | Primary action, hover, focus ring. The full 50–900 ramp is declared |
| `surface` | Page background |
| `panel` | Cards and raised surfaces |
| `elevated` | A surface on top of a panel — menus, hovered rows |
| `line` | Dividers and outlines |
| `ink` | Body copy |
| `ink-soft` | Labels, hints, timestamps |
| `ink-faint` | Placeholder and disabled text |
{% endif %}

The accent is an accent, not the palette. It marks the one thing on a screen
that should be clicked; a page where three things carry it has no accent at all.

Destructive actions share that weight, which is why a destructive button is
**outlined**, never solid — solid is already taken by "proceed".

The neutrals carry a hint of blue rather than being pure grey. Next to a
saturated accent, a perfectly neutral grey reads as dirty.

## Type

One family, from the token{% if is_web %} `--font`{% endif %} — the system UI
stack. Do not add a web font without saying so: it is a render-blocking request
and a licence question, not a style tweak.

Two sizes on a screen is usually right. Four is a screen that has stopped
having a hierarchy. Emphasis is weight and size, never colour.

## Spacing and shape

{% if is_web %}
- Spacing is `var(--space)` and multiples of it: `calc(var(--space) * 2)`. Not
  arbitrary pixels.
- Radius is `var(--radius)`, except badges and avatars, which are pills.
{% else %}
- Spacing steps: `2 / 3 / 4 / 6 / 8`. Not arbitrary pixels.
- Radius: `rounded-lg` for cards and inputs, `rounded-md` for buttons,
  `rounded-full` for badges and avatars.
{% endif %}
- **Borders over shadows on dark surfaces.** A shadow on near-black is
  invisible, so the border is what makes a card a card.
- Transitions: ~150ms, on colour, background, border and shadow only. An
  interface that animates its layout feels slow.

## The two states people forget

**Loading is not the word "Loading...".** Use a skeleton shaped like the
content that is coming, so the layout does not jump when it arrives.
{% if is_web %}HTMX sets `.htmx-request` on the element while a request is in
flight; that is the hook.{% endif %}

**Empty is not an empty page.** An empty list says what would be there and
offers the action that creates the first one.

## Verification

Before calling a screen done:

- Does it render in both themes? There are three states, not two: system,
  explicit `data-theme="dark"`, explicit `data-theme="light"`. Check all three.
- Is every colour a token?
- Does the focus ring show on keyboard navigation?
- Is there a loading state and an empty state?
- At 375px wide, does anything scroll the page sideways? Wide content scrolls
  inside its own container.

## Common mistakes

- **A raw colour in a component.** Add the token instead.
- **Colour used for emphasis.** Emphasis is weight and size. The accent is for
  the action.
- **`outline: none` with no replacement.** Keyboard users lose the page.
- **Colour as the only signal.** A red badge also says "Failed" in words.
- **An icon-only button with no `aria-label`.** It is unreadable to a screen
  reader and to anyone who has not memorised the icon.
{% if not is_web %}
- **A `dark:` class in a component.** The token already changes with the theme.
  A component that hardcodes both halves is two themes waiting to diverge.
{% endif %}
